---
title: "Infrastructure Portal — the QA Manager's release process"
---
flowchart TD
    classDef qam fill:#1f6feb,stroke:#0d419d,color:#fff
    classDef qa fill:#6f42c1,stroke:#4c2889,color:#fff
    classDef gate fill:#9e6a03,stroke:#7d4e00,color:#fff
    classDef good fill:#238636,stroke:#196c2e,color:#fff
    classDef bad fill:#a40e26,stroke:#7a0b1c,color:#fff
    classDef quiet fill:#3d444d,stroke:#6e7681,color:#fff

    START["`A component is built and reaches an environment`"]
    START --> WHICH{"`Which move is this?`"}:::gate
    WHICH -->|"`Dev to Test — early internal moves`"| SILENT["`Goes through on its own.
Nothing reaches the QA Manager.`"]:::quiet
    WHICH -->|"`Stable or Test to Staging,
or Staging to Production`"| PROMO

    PROMO["`A **Promotion** appears in the portal —
one component waiting for release.
The changes inside it are its **Work Items**.`"]
    PROMO --> LOOK
    NEW["`A newer build of the same component
arrives before this one is approved —
it replaces the older Promotion,
but sign-offs already given still count.`"]:::quiet
    NEW -.-> PROMO

    LOOK["`**QA Manager** opens **Promotions** and picks an
environment to see what is waiting there. Each row
shows how many changes are verified, and with what result.`"]:::qam
    LOOK --> OWNERS

    OWNERS{"`Does every change
have a **QA Owner**?`"}:::gate
    OWNERS -->|"`Yes — taken automatically from Jira`"| REVIEW
    OWNERS -->|"`No`"| VOL["`Unassigned changes sit under
**Work items queue → Not assigned**.
QA Manager asks for volunteers, or uses
**Assign** to put someone on as QA Owner.`"]:::qam
    VOL --> REVIEW

    REVIEW["`Each QA Owner tests their change on Staging from
**Work items queue → Assigned to me**
and records one of three results.`"]:::qa
    REVIEW --> R1["`**Approve** ✔
it works`"]:::good
    REVIEW --> R2["`**Issue** ⚠
a problem was found,
but it does not stop the release`"]:::gate
    REVIEW --> R3["`**Block** ⛔
this must not go out`"]:::bad

    R1 --> CLEARED
    R2 --> CLEARED
    CLEARED["`The change counts as **cleared**. An issue is
recorded with a comment and a link to Jira, so the
known problem travels with the release instead
of holding it.`"]:::quiet

    R3 --> HELD
    HELD["`The change counts as **not cleared**. A comment
explains why, with a link to Jira. The Promotion is
not cancelled — it waits, and the reviewer
can change their mind later.`"]:::quiet
    HELD -.->|"`fixed and re-tested`"| REVIEW

    CLEARED --> TARGET
    HELD --> TARGET
    TARGET{"`Where is this
Promotion going?`"}:::gate

    TARGET -->|"`To **Staging**`"| SOFT["`QA Manager may approve at any time.
Verification is visible here, but not required.`"]:::qam
    TARGET -->|"`To **Production**`"| HARD
    HARD{"`Is **every** change
inside it cleared?
Approved or Issue — only a
**Block** holds it, and so does a
change nobody has checked yet.`"}:::gate
    HARD -->|"`No`"| WAIT["`**Approve** stays locked. The portal names
the changes still blocked or unchecked, so
the QA Manager knows who to chase.`"]:::bad
    WAIT -.->|"`last outstanding change cleared`"| HARD
    HARD -->|"`Yes`"| CLEAR["`**Approve** unlocks. Only **Pawel Krainski** or
**Tatyana Velikanova** may give this
approval — one of them is enough.`"]:::good

    SOFT --> DECIDE
    CLEAR --> DECIDE
    DECIDE{"`QA Manager's decision`"}:::qam
    DECIDE -->|"`Reject`"| REJ["`The Promotion is stopped.
It will not be deployed.`"]:::bad
    DECIDE -->|"`Approve`"| UNDO

    UNDO["`Approved.
A short grace period follows, so the approval
can still be taken back if it was a mis-click.`"]:::gate
    UNDO -.->|"`taken back`"| DECIDE
    UNDO -->|"`grace period passes`"| SHIP["`The deployment starts automatically.
Nobody has to trigger it by hand.`"]:::good
    SHIP --> DONE["`Once the component is confirmed running on the
target environment, the Promotion closes
itself as **Deployed**.`"]:::good
